Kai's Character and Casey-M's characters

Kai's character: A Golden Dragonborn Monk who lived his life up until very recently in a monastary along the southern edge of the Duchy of Durmista. Living in harmony with their surroundings, caring for and participating in the pastoral life of the local farming communities, catering to travelers along the road connecting Durmista and the southern settled lands of Tethyr.

One evening, after his daily training and meditations, he ventured out alone and lit a modest bonfire on the edge of the forest (with his breath, being a dragonborn of course).

He then sat and played his flute, letting his music carry him deeper and deeper into himself-- exploring the depths of connection to the world through his song, and losing himself...
Quite literally. It was as though the forest grew around him, and the light from the fire faded away, and away, and he, being the introspective and deeply curious type, leaned into the sensation.

It was what felt like hours of this before he allowed himself to resurface from this trance... and it was then that he realized that something was different. The world around him was a different place. His fire that he had lit was gone.
The trees he had been sitting beneath had vanished and were replaced by others not familiar. The smell of this place was different, fresh and wild.

Rather perplexed, he decided to fly above the trees (with his wings, being a dragon of course) and found himself looking out a territory stretching out around him as far as he could see, which he had never gazed upon before. And an ocean to his North!

After his wings tired, he returned to the ground and with his ever-sanguine temperament began to walk through the forest toward the ocean.

It was a while later that he came upon a curious creature: a petite elvish woman, with a tiny bat companion, and most-strangly, a sentient log that followed her around much like a dog would. (Cornbread is her name). After cordial introductions, and Kai (I'll get these names right later) explaining what had happened to him, Cornbread (Casey) said something along the lines of "Oh yeah, that'll happen! That's happened to me a few times! I like it. I like to wander to new places."

They decided, rather naturally, that they would be quite alright wandering together for a while. And so they did, carrying on just a little farther to the ocean.